  "body": "## T-2383 \u2014 the Sauganash's boxed gable cornice\n\n**One visible partial increment on the original T-2383.** The ticket stays **open and\npartial**: this is not a full image match, not a sign-off, not a split, not a done\noverride, and no photo follow-up ticket is filed.\n\n### What the picture shows\n\nF. Braunhold's engraving in Andreas 1884 (`andreas_1884_sauganash_hotel_plate`) draws a\n**boxed cornice following both rakes of the hotel's visible main gable**, carrying its own\nsoffit, and at each eaves corner a **short horizontal return** turning onto the gable wall\nand stopping. Read on the plate at full size, both are unmistakable. The model built\nneither: the gable ran bare clapboard straight into the roof plane \u2014 a missing element a\nvisitor on the street would notice, which is `open` under T-3153's bar.\n\n### What this ships\n\n* `generators/archetypes/frame_tavern_params.py` \u2014 a new **default-off**\n  `main_gable_cornice` control: `{end, return_m, section_m, projection_m}`. `validate()`\n  refuses it at any confidence but `reconstructed`, refuses a non-gable roof, a scheme\n  whose gables are not at the x ends, a gallery, an end that is not `+x`/`-x`, a\n  non-finite or out-of-bounds section, returns that would meet across the end, a soffit\n  dropping into the storey below, and a band that would cross a sash the record already\n  states on that end (wall or attic).\n* `generators/archetypes/frame_tavern.py` \u2014 `_main_gable_cornice()`: two rake prisms from\n  each eaves corner to the apex, two returns running inward at the eave line, in the\n  existing **white wall material**, hanging **below** the rake line. The face coincident\n  with the gable triangle is left off rather than drawn into a z-fight. Winding is decided\n  from the geometry (`_face`), so the mirrored `-x` copy cannot come out inside-out.\n* `data/structures/sauganash_hotel.json` \u2014 the attribute on `frame_1831` only:\n  `end: \"+x\"`, `return_m 0.55`, `section_m 0.18`, `projection_m 0.18`, confidence\n  **reconstructed**.\n* `docs/LIBERTIES.md` **L-sauganash-main-gable-cornice-2383** + `data/liberties.json`,\n  the dossier section, `docs/STATUS.md`, and one `changelog.d/T-2383.json` entry.\n\n### Provenance \u2014 what is read and what is invented\n\nThe **occurrence and the form are read off the picture**. The **three sections are not**.\nThe plate is a retrospective 1884 engraving whose only scale datum is a standing man \u2014 the\nsame datum the 9.92 m frontage rests on. Measured on it, the drawn return reads **about\n0.86 m** against the gable's own eaves-to-eaves width and **about 0.71 m** against the\n0.85 m attic sash, with several tenths of a metre of line-weight and perspective\nuncertainty either way. The built **0.55 m** sits at the conservative end of that range and\nis a **working choice, not a measurement**; so are the 0.18 m section and projection,\nbounded only by the plate showing a band plainly deeper than a clapboard course (0.114 m)\nand plainly shallower than the entrance cornice already built. Nothing upgrades a\nconfidence, no source is invented, and **nothing is built on the opposite, unseen gable**.\n\n### Protected, and verified unchanged\n\n9.92 \u00d7 8 m footprint \u00b7 5.5 m wall \u00b7 25.2\u00b0 pitch \u00b7 UTM 447174.1 / 4637265.2, bearing 0 \u00b7\nevery opening and bay, the four lower sash, the entrance case and leaf, the blue louvred\nshutters, the two stacks, the 8 m cross wing, grades and paint \u00b7 the separate Carpenter\nshop. A unit test asserts the build is **purely additive**: every face the hotel already\nhad comes out unchanged, in place, with the same material and confidence, and exactly 16\nfaces are added.\n\n### Native build \u2014 genuinely rebuilt, not hash-renewed\n\nChanging the producer stales the whole family. **All 23 `frame_tavern` structures and the\ntwo Tremont version meshes were actually rebuilt** through the pinned Blender 4.5.3 on this\nworker (`generators/build.py --only <23 ids>`), before the first source commit, and their\nderivatives re-encoded (`tools/web_derivatives.sh --only` over the 25 masters it wrote).\n**Only `sauganash_hotel__frame_1831.glb` moved a byte** \u2014 which is what `default-off` means\nand is the check that it is off. No foreign manifest or `manifest.web` row was touched;\n`validate.py --stale` is clean.\n\n### Image review \u2014 four controlled renders, all directly reviewed\n\n| view | anchor | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `sauganash_hotel/andreas-1884` | hotel | **differs** (unchanged) \u2014 the cornice is recorded `fixed`; the compound roof silhouette and left-gable questions stay **open** |\n| `philo_carpenter_log_shop/andreas-1884` | shop | **matches**, retained |\n| `philo_carpenter_log_shop/trowbridge-1902` | shop | **matches**, retained |\n| `philo_carpenter_log_shop/kurz-allison-1893-panel14` | shop | **matches**, retained |\n\nAll four were re-rendered from their own controlled cameras with `tools/photo_match.mjs`\nand the new pairs were **looked at**, beside the images they replace, before any verdict was\nset. The hotel's new side-by-side shows the boxed band and both returns where the plate\ndraws them; the previous one shows the bare rake. The three shop verdicts are retained on\nthat review, not inherited: the shop **anchor** is byte-identical \u2014 its master, camera,\nplacement, openings and materials are untouched \u2014 and only the hotel behind it changed. A\nfresh `context_refresh_review` on each record says exactly that. No `groupSHA` was rewritten\nwithout a render, the hotel is **not** marked `matches`, and the already-done shop original\nis not reopened.\n\n### Verification\n\n* `tools/test_frame_tavern_picture_features.py` \u2014 25 tests, green, including three new ones:\n  the additive/geometry/orientation assertions, the default-off sweep over every\n  `frame_tavern` record, and the refusal table.\n* `./tools/check.sh --part 1/4 \u2026 4/4`, run in the foreground, one call each.\n  **Part 4 green.** Parts 1 and 3 each failed once on something this change genuinely\n  caused and both were fixed and re-verified: the Andreas plate's source-use backlinks\n  (`compile_source_use.py` \u2192 `SOURCE USE PASS`) and the register deal's undeclared note key\n  (`name_pool_keys.json` \u2192 `replace_invented_residents.py --check` OK). **Part 3 re-run is\n  green but for one step; part 2 has two.** All three are **artefacts of this worker, not of\n  this change**, and are stated rather than read as passes:\n  * `Every selected natural-standing derivative reproduces from its exact canonical parent\n    (T-1790)` and its part-3 twin \u2014 `human_natural_idle.py` does `git show\n    623eccd8\u2026:chicago/4d/assets/humans/\u2026`, and this checkout is a **`--depth 1` clone** (the\n    repository is 14 GB; a full clone did not finish), so that commit is simply not here.\n  * `Selected upper-lid source preserves 925/eyeUV/hoof ownership \u2026 (T-3088)` \u2014\n    `tools/transport/horse_socket_interface_v1/socket_controls.py` calls `np.cross` on 2-D\n    vectors, removed in NumPy 2.x; this runner has 2.x. Nothing in the diff reaches that file.\n\n  None of the three touches this change's domain. **The authority on the final head is the\n  hosted whole-source `gate` check on this PR**, which runs the same complete gate in eight\n  parts on a full clone with CI's own pins, and this PR is not merged until it is green.\n* Smoke, by parts, against the published mirror, in the foreground, each redirected to a\n  file \u2014 see the comment below for the measured subset and both-viewport results.\n\n### Limits\n\nThe hotel's own picture comparison still reads **differs**. The compound roof silhouette and\nthe remaining left-gable questions are open on their own merits, camera uncertainty stays\n`within tolerance`, and T-2383 is **released partial**, not done.\n",
